---
description: Dotfile sync via chezmoi from this checkout into `$HOME` when the modified repository root is exactly `/workspace`; gated by a successful dry-run (exact commands below).
globs: home/**
alwaysApply: false
---

**When to run:** Execute the numbered steps below only if the path of the repository you are currently modifying is exactly `/workspace`. For Git repositories, confirm with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (must print `/workspace` with no trailing slash). If the workspace or repository root is anything else, do not run these chezmoi commands and ignore this rule.

1. `chezmoi init -S /workspace -D "$HOME" -n --apply`
2. `chezmoi init -S /workspace -D "$HOME" --apply` — run only after step 1 succeeds with acceptable output.
3. `chezmoi apply -S /workspace -D "$HOME" -n` then `chezmoi apply -S /workspace -D "$HOME"` — use instead of 1–2 when `init` is not appropriate; same dry-run gate before the second command.
